      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we have to keep `buccaneer` separate, something like this *might* work:\n\n```\n/* Copyright 2026 The ChromiumOS Authors\n * Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be\n * found in the LICENSE file.\n */\n\n#include \"common.h\"\n#include \"gpio.h\"\n#include \"hooks.h\"\n\nstatic void buccaneer_board_init(void)\n{\n\t/* \n\t * The helipilot baseboard defines WP as a standard input. \n\t * Buccaneer specifically requires a pull-up on this line. \n\t */\n\tgpio_set_flags(GPIO_WP, GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_PULL_UP);\n}\n/* \n * The baseboard board_init runs at HOOK_PRIO_DEFAULT.\n * We run at HOOK_PRIO_DEFAULT + 1 to ensure we overwrite the flags \n * after the base system has initialized the GPIO array.\n */\nDECLARE_HOOK(HOOK_INIT, buccaneer_board_init, HOOK_PRIO_DEFAULT + 1);\n```",
